'''Divine Cyclone''' (エンジェルサイクロン, ''Enjeru Saikuron'', '''Angel Cyclone''') is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] introduced in [[Oncoming Maelstrom (Expert)|Oncoming Maelstrom]]. It was added in [[Version 2.7 Update|Version 2.7]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Divine Cyclone
|image = E 112.png
|first appearance = [[Oncoming Maelstrom (Expert)|Wrath of Heaven]]<br>
'''ZL''': [[Theheckareyou Island|Sub-chapter 5 - Theheckareyou Island]]
|money drop = 3,000¢ - 11,850¢
}}

==Enemy==
Divine Cyclone's gimmick is being the first [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] to lack the [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait, requiring specialized [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel units]] to counter it. Beyond that, it has all the typical attributes of a Cyclone: non-stop attacks and extreme health and DPS offset by pitiful range and somewhat low speed.

==Strategy==
You can easily take advantage of its short range by using [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|cats with knockback]], [[:Category:Cats with Slow ability|slow]] or [[:Category:Cats with Freeze ability|freeze]] abilities against Angels. Examples of these are [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Stilts Cat]], [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Toaster]] or [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]], respectively. As for damage dealers, almost anything will work in [[Oncoming Maelstrom (Expert)|Oncoming Maelstrom]], [[Wrath of A-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of A-Cyclone]] and [[Tornado Carnival (Deadly)|Tornado Carnival]] if you can keep it pinned down, while in [[Revenge of A-Cyclone (Deadly)|Revenge of A-Cyclone]] you should focus on units that continually knockback the [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] from behind the frontlines.

